From d4189e6aa5a353e7c6fb89990d6db876252cd458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for yrn-mwathi)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:06:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Register aspirants by seat, open their area immediately, fix
 campaign opening on Supabase, delete test campaigns
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes "You aren't a member…" when opening a campaign, even as super-admin:
- Cause: Supabase can switch row-level security on for every table, including
  the shared campaign tables. Membership checks that ran inside a campaign
  (restricted role) then saw no campaigns. /tenancy/switch now checks with
  owner access, and startup adds a policy so the app's own restricted role can
  read shared tables (Supabase's anon/authenticated roles stay locked out).
  Each table's step is isolated so it can't stop campaign isolation starting.
- New POST /api/tenancy/campaigns/:id/open (admin): super-admins open any
  campaign; other admins are added as members (keeping the primary campaign).

Aspirant setup:
- "Register an aspirant": candidate name (required), affiliated party (typed
  freely, suggestions, empty = Independent), the seat they're vying for and
  its area, election date, profile. No organisation or campaign-name fields;
  the campaign is named "<candidate> — <seat>, <area>".
- After registering, the aspirant's campaign opens on My Area with that seat's
  data: MCA → ward, MP → constituency, Governor/Senator/Woman Rep → county.
- Clicking any campaign opens it; "Details & members" holds edit, Add members
  and the new "Delete permanently".

Delete permanently (DELETE /api/tenancy/campaigns/:id, admin): exact name
required; removes every row the campaign owns (children before parents, from
the live foreign keys) in one transaction; never the primary campaign; parties
left without campaigns are removed.

Verified: 80/80 acceptance tests, typecheck + production build, and an end-to-
end run with row-level security on the shared tables (reproducing production):
switch works for super-admin; MP (Kitui West: 4 wards, 125 centres) and Woman
Rep (Kitui County: 40 wards, 1,320 centres) register and open; delete refuses
wrong names and the primary, then removes the campaign and all its rows.
